WEBVTT

Hello
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:15.100
Hello everyone. This one is real. On a Sunday night in August, a volunteer pointed a radio at the sky and caught 4 minutes of a satellite. The record for it says two words. with-signal.

Title
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.900
Nobody went back to it. It is one of two thousand seven hundred and twenty seven.

Problem
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:30.700
Only seven hundred and thirty nine carry a human verdict. The rest were kept and never read, because there is no order to work through them in.

Physics
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:55.900
A pass shifts the frequency you hear. The orbit predicts that curve, spanning seventeen thousand two hundred and ninety hertz. Slide it one hundred and thirteen pixels and it lands on the trace. The gap, as a fraction of the frequency, is plus thirty two point zero five parts per million. This station had already corrected for Doppler, and nothing in the record says so.

Queue
00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:07.100
That is what the queue ranks on. four hundred and seven observations against a budget of 50. Not the loudest. The ones where the evidence disagrees with itself.

Live
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:21.100
All of that was frozen in August. Here is the live console measuring one again. Of 10 quantities, 8 match the archived digits exactly.

Flow
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:37.700
You can drive the same evidence from a LangFlow canvas. Watch. A sentence goes in with a frequency this observation does not have. One take, no cut. The checker refuses it and names why.

Session
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:44.700
ungrounded number. That is the same checker that decides whether our own generated notes ship.

Result
00:01:45.350 --> 00:02:04.100
Now the part demos skip. Six gates, with thresholds, written before anything was measured. The headline one wanted half again as many conflicts as random. This queue found 20 of them. Random ordering, at the same budget, expects 12.6. We publish that as not established.

Gates
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:13.500
The point estimate is 1.58, and the interval straddles the bar, so it fails here. 3 of 6 gates met, and nothing was moved.

Established
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:28.100
Three did come back decided. Evidence tools take a local Granite model from 2 of 24 right to 22. The checker caught every one of five hundred and twenty five planted falsehoods. And on stations the queue never saw, lift clears at 2.25.

Bob
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:40.500
IBM Bob built the load-bearing pipeline: contracts, snapshot, parser, corridor, baselines, queue. 10 dated units, each naming what it changed and what failed first.

Colophon
00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:47.500
Every figure you heard came out of a receipt. The waterfall is public, cited and licensed.

Thanks
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:53.100
That is TraceTriage. Thank you for watching. Go and check a number.
